/* ============================================================================
   exponential-regression.epher -- fit y = a * e^(b x) to growth data

   Fits the least-squares exponential curve y = a * e^(b * x) to the
   culture sizes in `ys` sampled hourly in `xs` with the builtin expreg
   (guide 1.20), which prints the fitted model and the correlation r of
   the log-transformed fit as a display string. Unrestrained growth
   doubles in size at a steady rate, so an exponential fits well; the
   fitted b = 0.6766 per hour is a doubling about every hour. The data
   are illustrative example values, not measurements.

   Run it from a terminal:
     Linux (deb, rpm):  epher /usr/lib/epher/scripts/statistics/regression/exponential-regression.epher
     Windows:           epher "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\epher\scripts\statistics\regression\exponential-regression.epher"
     macOS:             epher /Applications/epher.app/Contents/Resources/scripts/statistics/regression/exponential-regression.epher
   In the REPL:             load one of the paths above
   Web/desktop:             paste the whole file into the entry, press Enter
   Everything also works line by line in the TUI.

   The knobs to edit are `xs` and `ys` below. Everything above the results
   section is machinery you can leave alone.
   ============================================================================ */

// ---- the knobs -----------------------------------------------------------------
const xs = {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5}   // hours since the culture was started
const ys = {1.0, 2.2, 3.9, 8.1, 15.6, 30.4}   // yeast culture size, grams

// ---- the fitted exponential -----------------------------------------------------------
expreg(xs, ys)      // least-squares exponential, printed with its r

/* ---- expected output ----
= {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5}
= {1, 2.2, 3.9, 8.1, 15.6, 30.4}
= y = 1.0434*e^(0.6766*x) (r = 0.9995)
*/